From c4d9c7791181b586bd27e1bcb57a28ae5c6be095 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rinehart <johnrichardrinehart@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 18:45:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: configure faint text opacity

Faint text always uses a fixed 50 percent foreground blend. KiTTY uses 40 percent, so the rendered result differs.

Add a faint-opacity setting and pass it to each renderer. Keep 0.5 as the default so the patch has no effect unless configured.
---
 dist/monstar.5       |  5 +++++
 src/App.zig          |  4 ++++
 src/AsyncRaster.zig  | 13 ++++++++++++-
 src/Config.zig       |  7 +++++++
 src/Renderer.zig     | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/bench.zig        |  2 +-
 src/pixel_raster.zig | 27 +++++++++++++++++++--------
 7 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dist/monstar.5 b/dist/monstar.5
index a28c166..932c63a 100644
--- a/dist/monstar.5
+++ b/dist/monstar.5
@@ -164,6 +164,11 @@ decodes sRGB colors, blends them in linear RGB with the original glyph
 coverage, and encodes the result as sRGB.
 The default is
 .BR default .
+.TP
+.BI faint-opacity " = opacity"
+Set the foreground opacity for faint text.
+The value is between 0 and 1 inclusive.
+The default is 0.5.
 .SH WINDOW SETTINGS
 .TP
 .BI background-opacity " = opacity"
